    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "number": "5.",
          "text": "Confirm that there are no fuel leaks after performing maintenance on the fuel system.",
          "subitems": [
            {
              "letter": "(a)",
              "text": "With engine stopped, turn the ignition switch on."
            },
            {
              "letter": "(b)",
              "text": "Short circuit terminals of the fuel pump check connector."
            },
            {
              "letter": "(c)",
              "text": "When the pressure regulator fuel return hose (shown in the figure at left), is pinched, the pressure within the high pressure line will rise to about 4 kg/cm² (57 psi, 392 kPa). In this state, check to see that there are no leaks from any part of the fuel system."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "caution",
      "text": "CAUTION: Always pinch the hose. Avoid bending as it may cause the hose to crack."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "TROUBLESHOOTING"
    },
